 "result": "`test_discount_rounding` passes now. I changed the code and left the test alone.\n\n**Cause:** in `calc/pricing.py:7`, `apply_discount` used `int(...)` to get to two decimal places, which cuts off digits instead of rounding. In floating point, `2.30 * 0.5 * 100` comes out as `114.99999\u00e2\u20ac\u00a6`, which got cut down to `114`, so the function returned `1.14` instead of `1.15`.\n\n**Fix:** that line is now `return round(price * (1 - pct / 100), 2)`. Prices now round to the nearest cent instead of always going down.\n\n**Test run:** pytest isn't installed here, so I used `python -m unittest`. `test_discount_rounding` passed, and so did the other test in `tests/test_pricing.py`, `test_no_discount`.\n\nNothing is committed.",
